# Standalone applications

You will run Counter: a SQLite count, a page with Increment, and a patch
that updates the card. Rocci generates the server. You do not write
`main`.

Complete source: [Counter](/examples/counter/) ·
[Counter.rocci](/examples/counter/source/Counter-rocci/).

## Open SQLite

`@context` is the value generated `main` threads through handlers.
`@init` opens the database and creates the row. Failures here exit the
process. Components stay pure.

```rocci
@context { db : Sqlite.Db }

@init {
    db = Sqlite.open!(Sqlite.default_config(db_path))?
    { db: db }
}
```

The cataloged file also creates the `counter` table and a starting row.

## Return a document

`@get:view("/")` returns a full HTML document. The increment control is a
real `<button>` with an unquoted Rocci action. The card uses
`id="counter"` so the later patch has a morph target.

```rocci
<button data-on:click=@post("/actions/counter/increment")>
    Increment
</button>
```

## Patch the card

```rocci
@post:fragment("/actions/counter/increment") = |{ db }| {
    count = increment_count!(db)?
    counterCard({ count: count })
}
```

`?` on SQLite becomes a 500 if the query fails. There is no `@log` and no
logging from `@component`.

This first app is **one-shot**. Increment morphs `#counter` in the acting
tab only. Shared streams are [handlers](/docs/applications/handlers/).

## Run it

```sh
rocci run examples/rocci/standalone/counter --no-window --log-handlers
```

Open the printed URL (default `http://127.0.0.1:8000/`). You should see
the Counter page, GET `/` is 200, and the card has `id="counter"`. Click
**Increment**: the number in the card goes up. Drop `--no-window` to use
the native preview.

`rocci run` on that directory picks the unique entry. `rocci run
Counter.rocci` still names the primary and loads sibling modules.

Next: [Handlers](/docs/applications/handlers/).
